		<td width="150" align="left" valign="top" class="row1"><span class="name"><a name="17015"></a><b>Lanturias</b></span><br /><span class="postdetails">Terror of Unrest<br /><img src="images/Ranks/swords/3sword.gif" alt="Journeyman" title="Journeyman" border="0" /><br /><img src="images/avatars/8370879253e7de4223346a.jpg" alt="" border="0" /><br /><br />Joined: 21 Aug 2002<br />Posts: 212<br /></span><br /></td>
		<td class="row1" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=17015&amp;sid=f9d76b17d468c28985f72f1a89f572fb#17015"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Wed Sep 03, 2003 3:51 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: A new beginning.</span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=17015&amp;sid=f9d76b17d468c28985f72f1a89f572fb"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">The wood elf warrior pulled his cloak tighter around his body. "Foolish of me" he thought "I knew perfectly well I would end up here in Velious, and dressed for combat and not for warmth." He trudged on through the snow,  seeking the mystical book which would grant him passage into the Plane of Knowledge. His sister had said she would be waiting for him there. He had to see her before his search could begin. He knew he might never see her again. His hand slid into his pocket and pulled out his latest carving. An elven female, holding a male child. Nearly any craftsman in the land would marvel upon the likeness there....the characters made in the block of wood truly had life of their own. But the warrior saw only the imperfections, and thought again "I'm getting better, I admit it. But I will never equal my father."
<br />

<br />
~~~~~~
<br />

<br />
Meanwhile his sister trudged through the Plane of Knowledge, heading towards the Great Divide stone. She didn't notice the multitudes on the walkway with her and received a few cold stares for jostling them occasionally. Her mind was filled with pain. "How am I going to find him? I don't have any idea where to look. It wouldn't be so bad if he knew I was alive. But he must surely believe me dead...Tunare, I almost can't believe I am still alive. I thought for sure...but its okay. My brother thought of everything. I am still alive thanks to him."
<br />

<br />
~~~~~~
<br />

<br />
Meanwhile, the high elf enchanter leaned back on his stool outside Ak'anon. The gnome in front of him with the dyed blue hair and the penchant for giggling at random intervals and for no reason was beginning to make him nervous. "Whats that you say boy? MtV as the initials?" the gnome relayed. "NO!" the enchanter replied, now thoroughly terrified. "Heh, just yanking your chain, son. I know what I am doing." the gnome started giggling again. The enchanter reached up and brushed away several drops of sweat from his forehead. He would be much happier when he was out of this curious gnome's shop and back into Everfrost. "I owe my mother this much" he thought grimly. "I have no idea if I can still find what I am after, but if I can, a few goblins and ice giants will not stand in my way."
<br />

<br />
"All done sonny!" the gnome exclaimed and the enchanter gasped. He had been so busy in his thoughts he hadn't even felt the stranger metal rod touch his skin, though his left shoulder now throbbed from where the gnome had left his markings. The enchanter stood up and looked nervously at the spot, then breathing a sigh of relief when he saw that for all the gnome's eccentricity,  his work was magnificent. Standing up slowly, he accepted the bandage from the gnome, and payed him well for his service. Then the enchanter left the building, pulling the bandage over his shoulder and the letters marked there. 
<br />

<br />
In bright red, CA. And underneath, in a black flourish the letter L.<br />_________________<br />Master Lanturias Kyerme
